    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The system's manager declared a red alert for Visayas after a cascade of failures exposing systemic rot, including the tripping of a unit that exposed systemic fragility. This equipment failure, a technical fault from a power generation unit, was the tipping point for chronic neglect by power holders. Officials, enforcers of a fragile order, then forced austerity on the people to save the infrastructure via emergency load shedding. The result was a massive loss of capacity and a blackout risk increase, threatening darkness imposed on ordinary people.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [
        "how_fragments_expanded_to_contiguous_span"
      ],
      "fit": 0.91
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The site of systemic failure, Visayas, faced a predictable crisis ignored by authorities as seasonal heat drove demand into a thin operating margin. This high demand, part of a broader demand surge, was compounded by prolonged outages and generator failures, revealing collapsing infrastructure. The gatekeeper of a failing grid responded with a grid alert and emergency measures, but not before a power capacity loss exceeding 950 megawatts became unavailable, amplifying grid instability and blackout risks.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
          "why-2",
          "why-1",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [
        "how_fragments_expanded_to_contiguous_span"
      ],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "Officials, as decision-makers and enforcers of a fragile order, ordered emergency load management to keep a critical transmission line from overloading after the grid operator's power system alert. This action followed a critical failure that revealed vulnerability when Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2 tripped offline, a unit failure among multiple failures. The resulting megawatt shortage and power outage risk highlighted the fragility of the power sources in the island region.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
